<section
    id="learning-experience"
    class="project-section w3-padding-32"
    aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
        <h2 id="experience-heading">The learning experience</h2>
        <p>
            The course begins by explaining how the original panel discussion was
            expanded into a broader learning experience. Learners are informed
            that they will watch short excerpts, review current research, view
            selected external media, and respond to questions.
        </p>

     

        <p>
            Each of the four parts has its own learning objectives. Within those
            parts, learners alternate among panel clips, explanatory content,
            readings, interactive components, external videos, and reflection
            prompts. This structure reduces long periods of passive viewing and
            gives learners multiple ways to engage with the subject.
        </p>

        <p>
            The design supports both linear progression and review. Learners can
            use the player controls to move backward to previous material. On
            screens containing required interactive content, the forward control
            is withheld until the learner has accessed the available material.
        </p>

        <p>
            The overall combination of panel footage, supporting instruction,
            research, interaction, and reflection was designed to meet the
            required two-hour continuing education scope. The post-course quiz is
            completed separately in Blackboard.
        </p>


    </section>




